    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all 3 tests green (the only test class in the tree; `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` are support classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, the single place where owner intake rules live:\n\n1. **New `normalizeAddress` helper** \u2014 trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands the abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE` on a per-token basis. `null` or whitespace-only input normalizes to `\"\"`.\n\n2. **Applied on creation** \u2014 `prepareNewOwner` now normalizes the DTO's `address` in place as its first step, so:\n   - The **stored and returned** address is the normalized form (mapped from the normalized DTO).\n   - The **required-field check** (`validateRequiredFields`) runs *after* normalization, so an address that is blank only after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"`) is rejected with 400.\n   - **Household duplicate detection** (`rejectDuplicateHousehold`) and **household-id assignment** (`assignHousehold`) both read the already-normalized address.\n\n3. **Comparison helpers use the normalized form** \u2014 `findHouseholdMates` and `householdIdFor` now apply `normalizeAddress` to both the incoming and each existing owner's address, so household identity is compared on normalized values consistently (making the behavior robust even if a caller passed a raw address).\n\nJavadoc was updated to describe the new normalization step and the blank-after-normalization rule. The three acceptance tests (`coreNormalizesWhitespaceAndCase`, `functionalityExpandsAbbreviations`, `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize`) all pass.",
